fying and maintaining the pH of intracellular compartments (PubMed:26212330). Required at an early stage of receptor-mediated endocytosis (PubMed:26212330). (Microbial infection) Required at an early stage of both clathrin-mediated and clathrin-independent endocytic uptake of a diverse set of viruses, including dengue, West Nile, Sindbis, Rift Valley Fever, influenza, and human rhinoviruses (PubMed:26056282, PubMed:26212330)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}